{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SBCTg86veMDKzSzRwmxB7N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context carefully and propose tasks.\n\n## Project Analysis\n\n### Problem\ngo-unix-utils is an experiment in specification-driven development. It derives formal specs from C/Perl source code, generates Go implementations from those specs using an AI coding agent, and verifies parity against reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n### Architecture\n- **cmd/**: Go implementations of each utility\n- **pkg/testutils/**: Differential testing harness\n- **pkg/sys/**: Syscall abstractions (terminal width, file metadata, signals)\n- **pkg/format/**: Output formatting (columns, ANSI color, human-readable sizes)\n\n\n- **magefiles/**: Build targets\n- **docs/**: Specifications (PRDs, use cases, test suites)\n\n### Current State\nLooking at the roadmap and implementation status, rel01.0 is in progress with ts having its PRD, use case, and test suite complete but implementation still pending. The next releases are queued up: rel01.1 covers wc, cat, and sponge with PRDs done but use cases and tests still needed, while rel02.0 tackles ls core and du with similar gaps, and rel02.1 extends ls further with PRDs complete and test suites partially done.\n\n### What needs to be built next\n\nThe ts utility is the current focus with its use case actively being worked on and a test suite of 12 cases already in place. To move forward on rel01.0, I need to tackle three things in sequence: first the pkg/testutils implementation which serves as the differential testing harness that all utilities depend on, then the actual cmd/ts implementation, and finally the differential tests for ts itself. Since I can only create one task and pkg/testutils is the foundational piece that everything else builds on, that's where I should start—it has a complete PRD and nothing else can move forward without it.\n\nLooking at what prd001-testutils actually requires, I'm building a differential testing harness with a DiffTest struct that captures arguments, stdin, environment variables, expected exit codes, and normalization functions. The core functionality involves executing both binaries with identical inputs, comparing their outputs byte-for-byte across stdout, stderr, and exit codes, and providing hooks for normalizing things like timestamps. There's also file-state comparison for utilities like sponge, cp, and mv. The implementation breaks down into manageable pieces—the struct definitions, the main test runner function, binary execution helpers, comparison and reporting logic, timestamp normalization, and file-state comparison—totaling around 280 lines of well-scoped work.\n\nThis fits the target, so I should focus purely on the implementation without mixing in tests, keeping the task focused on pkg/testutils itself. I'll structure it across a couple of files to keep concerns separated.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":76943,"cache_read_input_tokens":15594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":76943},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4246158-91ad-4b1c-975c-06af2c84ea72","uuid":"ed60d2ab-e6c9-408a-b846-a91729b75a10"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SBCTg86veMDKzSzRwmxB7N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project Analysis\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is a specification-driven development experiment that regenerates classic Unix utilities in Go, deriving formal specs from C/Perl source and verifying parity against GNU reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go binaries), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `magefiles/` (build targets), `docs/` (specs).\n\n**Current state**: All PRDs written for rel01.0 through rel02.1. No Go implementation code exists yet. The rel01.0 use case (ts) is in_progress — PRD, use case, and test suite are written; implementation is pending.\n\n**Current release**: rel01.0 — one use case remains: `rel01.0-uc001-ts` (timestamp stdin lines via ts). This requires `pkg/testutils` (the differential testing harness) to be implemented first, since every utility's verification depends on it.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nThe dependency chain is: `pkg/testutils` → `cmd/ts` implementation → `cmd/ts` differential tests. The single highest-priority task is implementing `pkg/testutils` — the differential testing harness. It is the foundation for every utility in the project and blocks all verification work.\n\nScoping: prd001-testutils defines DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests, binary execution, comparison/reporting, normalization hooks (including TimestampNormalizer), and file-state comparison. This fits within ~280 lines of production code."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":76943,"cache_read_input_tokens":15594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":76943},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4246158-91ad-4b1c-975c-06af2c84ea72","uuid":"84ba38ae-e9bd-4578-a1b9-95adad455508"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SBCTg86veMDKzSzRwmxB7N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BvpupZBYeoyvogjfKcAdiT","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/petardjukic/WORKSPACE/go-unix-utils/.cobbler/measure-20260223-203515.yaml","content":"- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/testutils differential testing harness\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd001-testutils.yaml (the full PRD for pkg/testutils; defines DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests API, comparison logic, normalization hooks, and file-state comparison)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (components section — pkg/testutils responsibility and its role as the acceptance gate for every utility)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel01.0.yaml (test suite for ts — shows how TimestampNormalizer is used in practice and what the harness API looks like from a consumer's perspective)\n      - go.mod (module path and Go version)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/diff.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"DiffTest struct, Normalize function type, RunDiffTests entry point, binary execution, comparison and reporting logic\"\n      - path: pkg/testutils/normalize.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"TimestampNormalizer, ComposeNormalizers helper, and the Normalize function type if split from diff.go\"\n      - path: pkg/testutils/diff_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Unit tests for the harness itself using a simple echo/cat binary as both Go and reference binary\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - \"R1: Define a DiffTest struct per prd001-testutils R1.1-R1.4. Fields: Name (string, used as t.Run subtest name), Args ([]string), Stdin ([]byte, nil means no stdin/immediate EOF), Env ([]string, nil means inherit test process env), ExitCode (int, expected exit code — used only for documentation, actual comparison is between the two binaries), Normalize ([]NormalizeFunc where NormalizeFunc is func([]byte) []byte — nil or empty means no normalization), ExpectedFiles (map[string][]byte — maps output file paths to expected content for file-state comparison; nil means no file comparison).\"\n      - \"R2: Implement RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary string, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest). For each DiffTest, call t.Run(test.Name, ...) to create a named subtest. Within each subtest, execute both binaries with identical args, stdin, and env. Compare normalized stdout, stderr, and exit code. Report divergence per prd001-testutils R3.5.\"\n      - \"R3: Binary execution must use os/exec.Command. Set Cmd.Stdin from DiffTest.Stdin (use bytes.NewReader; if nil, do not set Stdin so the process gets immediate EOF). Set Cmd.Env from DiffTest.Env if non-nil; if nil, leave Cmd.Env nil (inherits the current process environment). Capture stdout and stderr separately via Cmd.Output() or separate buffers. Extract the exit code from the *exec.ExitError. Apply a configurable timeout of 10 seconds per binary invocation using context.WithTimeout. If either binary exceeds the timeout, fail the subtest with a clear timeout message per prd001-testutils R2.3.\"\n      - \"R4: Before comparing, apply the Normalize function chain (DiffTest.Normalize) to both binaries' stdout and stderr. Iterate the slice in order, passing output through each function. If the slice is nil or empty, use raw output. Per prd001-testutils R4.1-R4.3.\"\n      - \"R5: Compare normalized stdout byte-for-byte (bytes.Equal). Compare normalized stderr byte-for-byte. Compare exit codes exactly. Any difference fails the subtest. The failure message must include: the DiffTest Args, the Stdin content (truncated to 256 bytes if longer), reference binary stdout, Go binary stdout, reference stderr, Go stderr, and both exit codes. Per prd001-testutils R3.1-R3.6.\"\n      - \"R6: Implement TimestampNormalizer as a NormalizeFunc. It must replace common strftime timestamp patterns with a fixed placeholder string 'TIMESTAMP'. Patterns to match: syslog format ('Mon DD HH:MM:SS' where Mon is a three-letter month abbreviation), ISO-8601 datetime ('YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS' with optional fractional seconds and timezone), and epoch-with-microseconds ('NNNNNNNNNN.NNNNNN'). Use regexp.ReplaceAll. Per prd001-testutils R4.2.\"\n      - \"R7: Implement file-state comparison per prd001-testutils R5.1-R5.2. When DiffTest.ExpectedFiles is non-nil, after both binaries exit, read each file path from the map and compare its content byte-for-byte to the expected content. Report divergence in the same format as stdout divergence (showing expected vs actual file content).\"\n      - \"R8: When both binaries run without a specified working directory, create a per-test temporary directory (t.TempDir()) and set Cmd.Dir to it. Per prd001-testutils R2.5.\"\n      - \"R9: A passing test run must produce no output to the test process stdout or stderr. Only failing tests produce output. Per prd001-testutils R2.4.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - \"Package name: package testutils. Import path: github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n      - \"NormalizeFunc type defined as: type NormalizeFunc func([]byte) []byte\"\n      - \"ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc returns a single function that applies each fn in order. This is a convenience for test authors.\"\n      - \"Use context.WithTimeout for the 10-second binary execution timeout. Cancel the context after each binary invocation.\"\n      - \"For exit code extraction: if err is nil, exit code is 0. If err is *exec.ExitError, extract ExitCode() from the ProcessState. If err is another type (e.g., binary not found), fail the test with the error message rather than comparing outputs.\"\n      - \"TimestampNormalizer uses compiled regexp.Regexp variables (package-level var, compiled once via regexp.MustCompile) for performance.\"\n      - \"The harness does NOT build or install binaries. Test files in cmd/ packages are responsible for building the Go binary (via go build or exec.Command with go run) and locating the reference binary (via exec.LookPath). The harness only executes pre-built binary paths.\"\n      - \"For diff_test.go: test the harness using the system 'echo' and 'cat' binaries (or a small Go test binary built in TestMain) as both the Go and reference binary, so tests pass without requiring any cmd/ implementation or Homebrew reference binaries.\"\n      - \"Do not use any external dependencies beyond the Go standard library. pkg/testutils has no dependency on golang.org/x/sys or any other external module.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - \"pkg/testutils/diff.go compiles with no errors\"\n      - \"pkg/testutils/normalize.go compiles with no errors\"\n      - \"go test ./pkg/testutils/... passes with no failures\"\n      - \"DiffTest struct has all fields specified in R1\"\n      - \"RunDiffTests creates named subtests via t.Run for each DiffTest\"\n      - \"A test where both binaries produce identical output passes silently (no output)\"\n      - \"A test where binaries produce different stdout fails with a message containing both outputs, the args, and both exit codes\"\n      - \"TimestampNormalizer replaces syslog-format timestamps (e.g., 'Feb 19 12:34:56') with the placeholder 'TIMESTAMP'\"\n      - \"TimestampNormalizer replaces ISO-8601 timestamps (e.g., '2024-02-19T12:34:56') with the placeholder 'TIMESTAMP'\"\n      - \"ComposeNormalizers applies multiple normalizers in sequence\"\n      - \"A test that exceeds the 10-second timeout fails with a clear timeout message\"\n      - \"golangci-lint runs clean on pkg/testutils/ (run: golangci-lint run ./pkg/testutils/...)\"\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":76943,"cache_read_input_tokens":15594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":76943},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4246158-91ad-4b1c-975c-06af2c84ea72","uuid":"ea43b70e-38d4-404d-aa0f-b939c112ce87"}
